        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "General procedure for 1–4: LH4 (0.040 g, 0.11 mmol) and LnCl3·6H2O (0.22 mmol) were combined in methanol (25 mL) to give a clear yellow solution and stirred 15 min at room temperature. Et3N (0.55 mmol) was added dropwise, then H2O2 (34.5–36.5%, 0.11 mmol) and pivalic acid (0.22 mmol). The mixture was stirred overnight at room temperature, filtered, and the solvent removed in vacuo. The yellow residue was dissolved in methanol with a few drops of chloroform and left undisturbed; crystals formed by slow evaporation in 3–4 days. For 1: LH4 (0.040 g, 0.11 mmol), GdCl3·6H2O (0.083 g, 0.22 mmol), H2O2 (0.11 mmol), pivalic acid (0.22 mmol), Et3N (0.55 mmol).",
